---
import ServiceSection from "../components/ServiceSection.astro";
import Endpoint from "../components/Endpoint.astro";
import RustSchema from "../components/RustSchema.astro";
---

<ServiceSection id="service-auth">
  <Fragment slot="title"><code>Auth</code> — authentication</Fragment>
<p>These plaintext endpoints bind the Sunken connection to the account and
    session authorized by Front. The cryptographic sequence is described in
    <a href="#resume">Native Resume authentication</a>.</p>
    <p class="endpoint-index">
      <a href="#auth-logon"><code>Auth/0</code> logon</a>
      <a href="#auth-resume-request">Auth/1 request</a>
      <a href="#auth-configuration">Auth/18 configuration</a>
      <a href="#auth-proof-request">Auth/2 request</a>
      <a href="#auth-proof-response">Auth/2 response</a>
      <a href="#auth-resume-response">Auth/1 response</a>
      <a href="#auth-web-token"><code>Auth/16</code> web token</a>
      <a href="#auth-sso"><code>Auth/17</code> SSO</a>
    </p>

    <Endpoint id="auth-logon" direction="bidirectional" phase="plaintext, alternate entry" structure="metadata order" status="implemented, alternate flow">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Auth/0</code> Authentication::Logon</Fragment>
      <p>Starts a cold native account logon. The normal connection flow uses Front
      followed by <code>Auth/1</code>.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`// client → server
struct LogonRequest3 {
    request_common: RequestCommon,
    account: Vec<u8>,
    compatibility: u32, // 0x000a16a7
}

// server → client
struct LogonResponse3 {
    result: LogonResult,
    raf: Option<RafState>,
}

enum LogonResult {
    Success(LogonSuccess),
    Failure(LogonFailure),
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="auth-resume-request" direction="client → server" phase="plaintext, first record" structure="logical order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Auth/1</code> Authentication::ResumeRequest</Fragment>
      <p>Starts native authentication with account identity and the version set for
      the SC2 game account selected on Front.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct ResumeRequest {
    common: RequestCommon,
    account: Vec<u8>,           // 3..=320 bytes
    game_account_region: u8,
    game_account_name: Vec<u8>, // 1..=32 bytes
}

struct RequestCommon {
    program: FourCC,
    platform: FourCC,
    locale: FourCC,
    versions: Vec<Version>, // count: 0..=63
}

struct Version {
    program_id: FourCC,
    component: FourCC,
    version: u32,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">The Base97563 macOS version records and compatibility
      number are listed in <a href="#resume">Resume authentication</a>. Account fields are
      private session material.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="auth-configuration" direction="server → client" phase="plaintext" structure="logical order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Auth/18</code> Authentication::Configuration</Fragment>
      <p>Supplies a small authentication configuration record before proof.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct Configuration {
    use_s3_depot: bool,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="auth-proof-request" direction="server → client" phase="plaintext" structure="logical order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Auth/2</code> Authentication::ProofRequest</Fragment>
      <p>Requests execution of up to four authentication modules. The array count
      occupies three bits and has the accepted range <code>0..=4</code>. Resume
      encodes count 2 for the thumbprint and session-proof modules.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`record AuthProofRequest {
    command_id: Bits<6> = 2,
    service_present: Bits<1> = 1,
    service_slot: Bits<4> = 0,
    payload: ProofRequest,
    final_alignment: byte,
}

struct ProofRequest {
    requests: ModuleRequest,
}

type ModuleRequest = Array<ModuleInput> {
    count_bits: 3,
    count_range: 0..=4,
}

struct ModuleInput {
    id: ModuleId,
    data: ModuleData,
}

type ModuleData = Blob {
    byte_count_bits: 10,
    byte_count_range: 0..=1023,
    alignment: byte,
}`} />
      <p id="auth-module-id"><b>The 40-byte module identifier</b> selects the authentication-module
      implementation that must interpret <code>data</code>. The Sunken routing header
      carries the separate six-bit <code>Auth/2</code> command ID.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct ModuleId {
    usage: [u8; 8],    // b"auth\\0\\0\\0\\0"
    identity: [u8; 32],
}

const THUMBPRINT_ID: [u8; 32] = [
    0xd7, 0xe6, 0x62, 0x40, 0x80, 0xc1, 0xab, 0xa6,
    0x6d, 0xee, 0x63, 0xa6, 0xf3, 0x92, 0x8d, 0x8a,
    0x54, 0x69, 0x25, 0x7f, 0x58, 0x20, 0xb5, 0x72,
    0x1f, 0xb8, 0xc3, 0x2b, 0x6b, 0x5b, 0xef, 0x5d,
];

const SESSION_PROOF_ID: [u8; 32] = [
    0x89, 0x50, 0x05, 0x34, 0x0a, 0x63, 0x0a, 0x64,
    0x65, 0xa6, 0x5f, 0xec, 0x96, 0x32, 0x3c, 0x31,
    0x0b, 0xca, 0x8a, 0x9f, 0x66, 0xec, 0xee, 0xb1,
    0x88, 0x7a, 0x9d, 0x6c, 0x0e, 0x67, 0x61, 0x2e,
];`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">Resume supplies these two modules in the order shown.
      The explicit three-bit count supplies their cardinality; the native schema
      delimits the complete record.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="auth-proof-response" direction="client → server" phase="plaintext" structure="logical order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Auth/2</code> Authentication::ProofResponse</Fragment>
      <p>Returns outputs requested by the authentication modules. The thumbprint
      module is verified locally and emits zero outputs. The Resume response
      therefore contains one session-proof output.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct ProofResponse {
    responses: Vec<ModuleOutput>, // count: 3 wire bits, valid 0..=4
}

struct ModuleOutput {
    data: Vec<u8>, // byte count: 10 wire bits, 0..=1023; then byte-align
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">The session-proof output is
      <code>01 || client_nonce[16] || proof[32]</code>, for a byte count of 49.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="auth-resume-response" direction="server → client" phase="plaintext" structure="logical order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Auth/1</code> Authentication::ResumeResponse</Fragment>
      <p>Completes Resume. A successful response contains the phase-two server
      proof. A failure contains an update, an error and wait pair, or a
      version-check disconnect.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct ResumeResponse {
    result: ResumeResult,
}

enum ResumeResult {
    Success {
        final_requests: Vec<ModuleInput>, // count: 3 wire bits, 0..=4
        ping_timeout: TimeDelta,
        regulator_rules: Option<RegulatorRules>,
    },
    Failure {
        strings: Option<[u8; 40]>,
        reason: ResumeFailure,
    },
}

enum ResumeFailure {
    Update(UpdateInfo),
    Failure { error: ErrorCode, wait: TimeDelta },
    VersionCheckDisconnect,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="auth-web-token" direction="bidirectional" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="capture decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Auth/16</code> Authentication::GenerateWebToken</Fragment>
      <p>Requests a web token using a client-generated correlation token. The
      response returns either token bytes or a 16-bit error.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`// client → server
struct GenerateWebTokenRequest {
    token: u32,
}

// server → client
struct GenerateWebTokenResponse {
    token: u32,
    result: Result<Vec<u8>, u16>,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">The same captured wire shapes are also named
      <code>GenerateAppTokenRequest</code> and <code>GenerateAppTokenResponse</code>
      in related generated interfaces. This route retains both known symbolic names.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="auth-sso" direction="client → server" phase="plaintext, alternate entry" structure="metadata order" status="implemented, alternate flow">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Auth/17</code> Authentication::SingleSignOnRequest3</Fragment>
      <p>Starts native authentication from an SSO identifier. The documented Front
      handoff uses <code>Auth/1 ResumeRequest</code>.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct SingleSignOnRequest3 {
    request_common: RequestCommon,
    sso_id: Vec<u8>,       // 1..=512 bytes
    compatibility: u32,   // 0x000a16a7
}`} />
    </Endpoint>
</ServiceSection>
